You are auditing a repair pass of the Harn release flow.
{{ if fixup_pr_url != "" -}}
The durable recovery source includes open Release PR `{{ fixup_pr_url }}`.
{{ else -}}
The durable recovery source is tag or immutable attempt `{{ fixup_tag }}`.
{{ end -}}
The harness proved one exact immutable recovery commit and recovered its
original pin with `git merge-base <publication-oid> origin/{{ base_branch }}`.

What the harness already did, deterministically:

- Recreated the local release branch on a fresh `{{ base_branch }}` snapshot.
  Existing attempt refs and tags remain immutable.
{{ if candidate_tree_notes -}}
- Restored both `CHANGELOG.md` and `changelog.d` from that fresh candidate
  tree, then folded its complete current note set into `## v{{ target_version }}`.
  This is a new pre-tag candidate, so every source change it contains must be
  represented in this release and `## Unreleased` should be empty afterward.
{{ else -}}
- Preserved the frozen artifact's release body, promoted its pin-time notes,
  and smart-subtracted those notes from current `## Unreleased`. Entries that
  landed after the frozen artifact remain for the next release.
{{ end -}}
- Reused only gates that origin already proves. An existing tag never moves;
  otherwise the deterministic ship stage will tag the new publication OID.

Constraints:

- Never recommend moving a tag or re-publishing an immutable artifact.
- Do not author a new release section or emit draft markers. The selected
  release-note source above is authoritative.
- Inspect the merged `CHANGELOG.md` and at least one PR, diff, or source file
  with local read-only tools before returning a short `Audit:` block.

Confirm that v{{ target_version }} matches the selected source without dropped,
duplicated, or truncated bullets. Flag any source change whose note is missing.
{{ if candidate_tree_notes -}}
Flag any residual `## Unreleased` entry or fragment: it should have been folded
into this fresh candidate.
{{ else -}}
Flag any `## Unreleased` entry that actually belongs to the frozen artifact;
otherwise confirm those entries describe later work.
{{ end -}}

Do not include `BEGIN_DRAFT_CHANGELOG` markers.

When calling a tool, `_nl_intent` may describe the exact read-only intent.
